## Useful evidence, honestly presented

:::::: {.bms-two-column}
::::: {.bms-prose}
Backgammon engines are useful, but they are not magic.

When the method matters, we show the assumptions, limitations, source code, sample sizes, and supporting data behind the result.

Some tools use public data from services such as OpenGammon. Public data does not mean that the service itself is open source.

Engine output is evidence, not an explanation. Where the evidence is limited, uncertain, or contested, we say so clearly.
:::::

::::: {.bms-principles}
- Show the evidence
- Explain the assumptions
- Make sample sizes visible
- Separate results from interpretation
- Correct mistakes openly
:::::
